{#- The review panel. Replaces the inline "Next review:" chip, which sat fourth
    in a row of stats and whose own CSS comment called it "deliberately as
    quiet as .horizon-note". It was missed entirely for weeks; the reader
    traded on every rank change instead of monthly. Everything here is
    required to be ABSOLUTE -- readable with no prior knowledge and nothing to
    compare against -- because the two signals that failed were both relative.

    All regions start empty and are filled by renderReviewPanel() client-side,
    never baked: a page built days ago must not state a stale review date. -#}
<section class="review-panel" id="review-panel" hidden>
  <div class="rp-headline" id="rp-headline"></div>
  <ul class="rp-actions" id="rp-actions"></ul>
  <div class="rp-footer">
    <span class="rp-count" id="rp-count"></span>
    <label class="rp-lock" id="rp-lock-wrap" hidden>
      <input type="checkbox" id="rp-lock">
      <span data-i18n="rp_lock_label">Lock book until the review</span>
    </label>
    <button type="button" class="review-done-btn" id="review-done-btn"
            data-i18n="review_done" hidden>Done ✓</button>
  </div>
  {#- A blocked star tap's VISIBLE channel. announceLive() (positions.js) is
      the screen-reader channel, and the `title` attribute it also sets needs
      a hover-dwell no touch device ever produces -- so on a phone, a blocked
      tap otherwise produces literally no visible change (positions.js's own
      "reads as a broken page" comment). This lives on the panel, not the
      star, because the star that was tapped may be on the (mobile-hidden)
      table row a click was forwarded FROM, not anything on screen -- see
      _renderMobileCardsNow()'s card-to-table forwarding. Hidden by default;
      positions.js unhides it for a few seconds per blocked tap. -#}
  <div class="rp-block-note" id="rp-block-note" hidden></div>
</section>
